{% from "macros/icons.njk" import kiGlyph %}
{#
  The Atlas's Field Guide, after the ki-design site preview (examples/site-preview/field-guide.html).

  The cards are rendered from src/_data/kiSymbols.json5, a vendored snapshot of the ki-design symbol
  library refreshed by `bun run --cwd apps/site sync:design`. The snapshot carries only official and agreed
  entries: proposed vocabulary is withheld at the sync, so no template here can publish a proposal beside
  official entries. The framing below — the group titles, their introductions and where the Voyage explains them — is
  this site's own and survives a refresh.

  The status chips read Official and Agreed (GDR-KI-DESIGN-002), styled by `badge-official` and
  `badge-agreed` in main.css, so each card's chip takes its class straight from the symbol's status.
#}
{%- set statusLabel = { official: "Official", agreed: "Agreed" } %}
{%- set groupInfo = {
  "geography": { title: "Geography", intro: "From realm to island: the shapes knowledge takes on the chart.", voyage: "The Wider Picture", href: "/#wider" },
  "zone": { title: "Zones", intro: "The places on every island.", voyage: "The Home", href: "/#home" },
  "structure": { title: "Structures", intro: "Buildings that stand for what an island does.", voyage: "The Home", href: "/#home" },
  "port-mode": { title: "Port modes", intro: "The ways knowledge reaches and leaves an island: the districts of one Port.", voyage: "The Cycle", href: "/#cycle" },
  "signal": { title: "Signals", intro: "Marks that ask for attention. Every signal has a shape and a word, never colour alone.", voyage: "The Cycle", href: "/#cycle" },
  "condition": { title: "Condition", intro: "How well a place is tended, from the freshness of its evidence. Never a score.", voyage: "The Foundation", href: "/#foundation" },
  "role": { title: "Roles", intro: "The hats an agent wears while tending an island. Any agent, human or AI, may wear one; a role names work, not authority." },
  "sea": { title: "The sea", intro: "Routes, currents and hazards between the islands.", voyage: "The Cycle", href: "/#cycle" }
} %}

<section class="page-head lattice-bg" data-theme="night" aria-labelledby="guide-title" style="background-color: var(--color-navy);">
  <div class="page-container">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Knowledge Islands</a> · The Atlas</p>
    <p class="kicker">The Atlas</p>
    <h1 id="guide-title" class="display-l">Field Guide</h1>
    <p class="lead">Every mark on the map, once: what it is, what it means, and whether it is settled. Return here whenever the Voyage names a place you want to look up.</p>
    <div class="status-key" aria-label="Status key">
      <div><span class="badge badge-official">Official</span> Ratified in Knowledge Islands Principal</div>
      <div><span class="badge badge-agreed">Agreed</span> Agreed, not yet enacted into Knowledge Islands Principal</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<nav class="guide-filters" aria-label="Filter symbols by group" hidden>
  <div class="page-container">
    <button class="chip" type="button" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All<span class="n">{{ kiSymbols.counts.published }}</span></button>
    {%- for group in kiSymbols.categories %}
    <button class="chip" type="button" data-filter="{{ group.id }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ groupInfo[group.id].title or group.id }}<span class="n">{{ group.symbols | length }}</span></button>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</nav>

<section class="section-parchment" aria-label="About these entries">
  <div class="page-container">
    <div class="prose-ki" style="padding-top: 3rem;">
      <p>An agreed entry has the owner's agreement but is not yet written into Knowledge Islands Principal, so the rest of this site still uses the enacted word. The Port shows how an entry becomes official: Principal's Symbol Library once listed Harbour, an integration point, and Port, operational systems, as two symbols, and the design system agreed to fold them into one Port with four modes. <a href="https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-principal/blob/25b30fec5993da2162fa21a60db0d3a8f5893133/Admin/Governance/Decisions/GDR-KI-PRINCIPAL-010-the-port.md">GDR-KI-PRINCIPAL-010</a> enacted it, retiring the Harbour, and split the Lighthouse, now guidance only, from the Council Hall, which means governance. <a href="https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-principal/blob/ff513b9bfa6551b0e7a40f2bcbecb74eb43ef7ec/Admin/Governance/Decisions/GDR-KI-PRINCIPAL-013-the-causeway-and-the-mill.md">GDR-KI-PRINCIPAL-013</a> made the Causeway the translation layer and added the Mill, and <a href="https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-principal/blob/ff513b9bfa6551b0e7a40f2bcbecb74eb43ef7ec/Admin/Governance/Decisions/GDR-KI-PRINCIPAL-014-steward-roles.md">GDR-KI-PRINCIPAL-014</a> made seven roles official. Entries still under discussion are not shown here.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="section-parchment">
  {%- for group in kiSymbols.categories %}
  {%- set info = groupInfo[group.id] %}
  <section class="guide-section" data-category="{{ group.id }}" aria-labelledby="group-{{ group.id }}">
    <div class="page-container">
      <header>
        <h2 id="group-{{ group.id }}" class="display-m">{{ info.title or group.id }}</h2>
        <p>{{ info.intro }}{% if info.href %} <a href="{{ info.href }}">Explained in the Voyage: {{ info.voyage }}</a>{% endif %}</p>
      </header>
      <ul class="sym-grid">
        {%- for symbol in group.symbols %}
        <li class="sym" id="sym-{{ symbol.id }}">
          {%- if symbol.icon %}
          <span class="roundel" aria-hidden="true">{{ kiGlyph(symbol.icon) }}</span>
          {%- else %}
          <span class="roundel empty" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ki-glyph" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 4 L18.9 8 V16 L12 20 L5.1 16 V8 Z" stroke-dasharray="2 2.4"/></svg></span>
          {%- endif %}
          <div>
            <h3 class="display-xs">{{ symbol.name }}</h3>
            <div class="sym-meta"><span class="badge badge-{{ symbol.status }}">{{ statusLabel[symbol.status] }}</span><code>{{ symbol.id }}</code>{% if not symbol.icon %} <span class="meta">No glyph yet</span>{% endif %}</div>
            <p>{{ symbol.meaning }}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}

  <div class="page-container">
    <div class="prose-ki" style="max-width: none; padding-bottom: 4rem;">
      {% include "partials/sources.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
